/-!
# What the printer needs to know about an extern

Generated by `scripts/gen-externs-meta.py` from `LakeJs/Externs.lean`; do not edit by
hand.  `Externs.cName` is the name of the runtime function a call prints as, and
`Externs.arity` is how many arguments that function takes — the number of arrows in the
type the catalogue gives the constructor, which is *not* the same as the number of
arrows in the `Ty` the constructor is applied at, since a type argument may itself be a
function type.
-/

